/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (As we embark on the momentous occasion of Cancer Institute \(WIA\) entering its 70th year of service, we take pride in reflecting upon the remarkable journey of the Department of Molecular Oncology. This transformative journey began in 1994 with foundational research and blossomed into an example of cutting-edge medical science, bridging the realms of basic and clinical research.)
/E (As we embark on the momentous occasion of Cancer Institute \(WIA\) entering its 70th year of service, we take pride in reflecting upon the remarkable journey of the Department of Molecular Oncology. This transformative journey began in 1994 with foundational research and blossomed into an example of cutting-edge medical science, bridging the realms of basic and clinical research.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Under the visionary leadership of Dr. T. Rajkumar MD., DM., PhD., DSc., FAMS, the Department of Molecular Oncology emerged as a pioneering force in the realm of cancer research. In 2012, the department translated its research into tangible patient care with the establishment of the Molecular Diagnostic Unit \(MDU\), marking a significant milestone in our commitment to advancing healthcare.)
/E (Under the visionary leadership of Dr. T. Rajkumar MD., DM., PhD., DSc., FAMS, the Department of Molecular Oncology emerged as a pioneering force in the realm of cancer research. In 2012, the department translated its research into tangible patient care with the establishment of the Molecular Diagnostic Unit \(MDU\), marking a significant milestone in our commitment to advancing healthcare.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (MDU, the first laboratory at Cancer Institute \(WIA\) to receive NABL accreditation in 2014, stands as a testament to our unwavering dedication to quality and precision in molecular diagnostics. Initially, a small team of four, led by Dr. Samson Mani, spearheaded the genomics facility, with Ms. Meenakumari, Ms. Sangeetha, and Mr. Pitchai Muthu contributing to sample collection and testing.)
/E (MDU, the first laboratory at Cancer Institute \(WIA\) to receive NABL accreditation in 2014, stands as a testament to our unwavering dedication to quality and precision in molecular diagnostics. Initially, a small team of four, led by Dr. Samson Mani, spearheaded the genomics facility, with Ms. Meenakumari, Ms. Sangeetha, and Mr. Pitchai Muthu contributing to sample collection and testing.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The journey began with a focus on BCR-ABL translocation qualitative analysis and EWS-FLI translocation analysis. Over the years, MDU's scope expanded, adding BCR-ABL translocation quantitative analysis and Next-generation sequencing for breast cancer gene panels in 2014. These advancements empowered clinicians in treatment management, with a particular emphasis on identifying germline and somatic variants in hereditary breast and ovarian cancer.)
/E (The journey began with a focus on BCR-ABL translocation qualitative analysis and EWS-FLI translocation analysis. Over the years, MDU's scope expanded, adding BCR-ABL translocation quantitative analysis and Next-generation sequencing for breast cancer gene panels in 2014. These advancements empowered clinicians in treatment management, with a particular emphasis on identifying germline and somatic variants in hereditary breast and ovarian cancer.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
