/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Triumph over Lymphedema: A Journey of Hope and Healing!)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mrs. Kamatchi's inspiring journey through lymphedema management stands as a testament to the compassionate care provided by the institute. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mrs. Kamatchi, a resilient 59-year-old woman, embarked on her journey with the Department of Physiotherapy following a complex medical history. Having undergone a Right-side breast excision in 2003 and subsequent diagnosis of malignant IDC-Grade 2, she sought further management at the Cancer Institute. Mrs. Kamatchi faced the aftermath of cancer treatments, including three cycles of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, leading to the development of marginal lymphedema in 2006. Over time, this lymphedema progressed, significantly impacting her quality of life.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Challenges Faced:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The consequences of gross lymphedema took a toll on Mrs. Kamatchi's emotional well-being and daily life. Struggling with depression, housebound, and feeling isolated due to body image issues, she sought refuge at the Department of Physiotherapy in the hope of finding relief.  The journey to recovery commenced with a three-week Complete Decongestive Therapy \(CDT\) regimen, complemented by home care lymphedema measures. As her condition improved, she underwent a limb reduction procedure. Following the successful healing of the wound, Mrs. Kamatchi continued her therapeutic path with a two-week Manual Lymphatic Drainage \(MLD\) therapy. She was advised to wear compression stockings regularly to sustain the progress achieved through the treatment.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 151 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Healing Process:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Under the guidance of Dr. Sridevi, Mrs. Kamatchi underwent a comprehensive lymphedema assessment and provided informed consent for her treatment plan. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 151 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Triumph Over Lymphedema:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Just one month after initiating the prescribed therapy, Mrs. Kamatchi experienced a remarkable reduction in her gross lymphedema, reaching a minimal level. Her journey with the Department of Physiotherapy had not only restored physical health but also rekindled hope and joy in her life. No longer confined to her home, Mrs. Kamatchi is now an active participant in her daily activities, enjoying the company of her family and grandchildren.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Through personalized care and innovative therapies, the institute continues to empower individuals to overcome the hurdles posed by cancer-related complications, reaffirming its position as a center of excellence in holistic cancer care.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
